^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
dropped the body
--
N5008 [temp.inst]/4 + [basic.def.odr]/5: naming `swap(declval<T &>(),
declval<T &>())' in an unevaluated operand (the decltype of a SFINAE
default template argument) instantiates the DECLARATION of swap<NoCopy>
only; the specialization is never odr-used, so its definition -- ill-formed
for a type with a deleted copy -- is not instantiated (g++/clang++ accept
the program).  The front end instantiated the definition anyway, failed on
the deleted copy and reported "dropped the body of function
'swap<tag-NoCopy>'" for a body no program can call (audit residue item 12,
round 162: cpp11_is_swappable_unevaluated).  Fixed in round 163: a
specialization instantiated while a decltype/noexcept operand is being
type-checked is held back like a conversion probe's (speculative_instances)
and its definition is converted only once a converted body refers to it.
